WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.440
Iron Man was the spark for the MCU's vast
cast of characters, but with the twisted tangle

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.660
of cosmic timelines, did you know he never
met some of the other heavy hitters?

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.260
Keep watching to see the 5 heroes Iron Man
never met in the MCU.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.860
Tony may have met Hank Pym, Janet Van Dyne,
and possibly even Peggy Carter when he was

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.860
younger.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.060
That's plausible.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:31.190
We saw Howard Stark and Hank working together
in both Endgame and the first Ant-Man movie.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.980
Even though they had a falling out with Howard,
it's nice that Hank and Janet attended Tony's

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.730
funeral in Endgame.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:42.690
In Marvel comics, Janet's Wasp and Tony's
Iron Man were co-founders of the original

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.449
Avengers and even dated for a little while.

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:46.940
That's another story.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.269
The only Ant-Man character Tony Stark has
met on-screen is Scott Lang, first towards

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:55.289
the end of Civil War and then later in Endgame.

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:59.760
After Hope Van Dyne comes through the portals
in Endgame, though, she doesn't really interact

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.030
with Iron Man.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.089
It's a bummer they didn't get a chance to
meet, especially since their parents were

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:06.089
coworkers.

00:01:06.089 --> 00:01:07.089
Then again, Scott Lang said,

00:01:07.089 --> 00:01:10.689
"Hank Pym always said you never can trust
a Stark."

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:14.520
toward Tony in Captain America: Civil War,
leading Tony to reply:

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.730
"Who are you?"

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:21.020
If Hope grew up hearing that too, then maybe
she wasn't interested in becoming pals.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:25.940
It's actually a plot point in Infinity War
that Tony Stark doesn't know who Gamora is

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.479
when he comes face to face with Peter Quill
and the Guardian squad.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:33.939
By the time Iron Man, Spider-Man, and Doctor
Strange meet up with them in Infinity War,

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:36.640
Gamora has already been kidnapped by Thanos.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.030
She dies on Vormir shortly thereafter.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.359
The "new" time-traveling 2014 version of Gamora
doesn't really get to meet Tony in Endgame,

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:45.359
either.

00:01:45.359 --> 00:01:51.229
This is kind of a shame for the MCU, especially
considering that Tony and Gamora absolutely

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:52.299
hooked up in a comic too.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:57.183
"If there’s one thing I’ve proven it’s
that you can count on me to pleasure myself.”

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:02.590
Black Panther's sister Shuri had a really
important role in Infinity War and got to

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.259
be Science Bros with Bruce Banner, but Iron
Man was in space at that time.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:12.790
It's possible that he hasn't met Okoye either,
but since she represented Wakanda at Natasha's

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.950
holographic Zoom meetings during the Blip
it's pretty likely that the Dora Milaje leader

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.500
has talked to Tony via hologram at the very
least.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.640
Even though he retired to the woods with Pepper
to raise Morgan in Endgame, he wasn't totally

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.980
off the grid.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.510
Shuri was taken by Thanos' snap, though, so
we know she wasn't around.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:37.790
This does, however, raise an interesting question:
has Tony Stark even been to Wakanda?

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:43.670
He got close during the vibranium heist in
Age of Ultron, but we have very little information

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.909
on what he knew about the secret nation and
its superscience.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:53.000
If T'Challa and Steve Rogers were harboring
Bucky Barnes in Wakanda in the aftermath of

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.209
Civil War, then they probably weren't expecting
Mr. Stark to visit any time soon.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:03.580
It sure looks like he missed out on the world
of Black Panther entirely.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:09.400
He never got to experience all of that advanced
technology, or Shuri's delightful personality.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.099
It would've been a real treat for fans to
listen to the two swap science stories.

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:19.989
Perhaps she could've even shown him a more
efficient way to make an Iron Man suit when

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:21.890
he was back in the cave.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.510
"Sometimes you gotta run before you can walk."

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.110
Peter Parker says to Valkyrie when they meet
in the final battle against Thanos,

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:32.540
"Hey, nice to meet you-- oh my God!"

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:37.360
Rocket Raccoon meets her in New Asgard when
they go to get Thor in Endgame.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.959
She becomes good friends with the Hulk during
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:45.530
But unless Tony took a trip to Norway we don't
know about during the five years that passed

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:50.430
in Endgame, Iron Man hasn't actually met Asgard's
newest monarch.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:56.209
He also hasn't met Lady Sif, the only surviving
member of Thor's pals, either.

00:03:56.209 --> 00:04:01.519
Nor has he crossed paths with Darcy Lewis
or even future superhero Jane Foster, for

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:02.610
that matter.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.959
Almost all of the characters Iron Man hasn't
met are women.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:09.159
Are you noticing that too?

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:13.910
Thankfully, representation in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe is changing and expanding with every

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:14.920
new entry.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.680
Plus, it's probably not intentional that Tony
didn't meet these women in the final battle.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.660
If you check out deleted scenes from Endgame,
there's a sequence in which Iron Man is seen

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.210
being honored as he dies by Wasp, Valkyrie,
and Okoye, among others, that didn't make

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.350
it into the film.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.000
Gamora opts out, by the way.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.190
Hard to say it counts, but it's certainly
something to think about.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.340
"Make your move, reindeer games."

00:04:41.029 --> 00:04:45.860
How the heck did Iron Man never meet Groot?

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:51.630
The sulking teenage tree is the second Guardians
character who hasn't interacted with Tony

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.630
Stark.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.900
In Infinity War, he was on a mission with
Thor and Rocket to forge a new hammer when

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.380
Tony met the other Guardians.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:04.680
Then Groot joined the Wakanda fight with Thor
and Rocket and got snapped away by Thanos.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.020
Tony returned to Earth in Endgame and met
Rocket Raccoon, who worked with him on the

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:11.870
Time Heist plan to retrieve the Infinity Stones.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:16.710
However, Groot didn't show back up until the
portals opened at the end of the film, missing

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.610
Tony completely.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:25.100
Imagine the jokes Iron Man would have made
if he really stopped to take notice of a sentient

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.830
sapling fighting beside him.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.490
At least we'll always have Cap formally introducing
himself to Groot in Infinity War.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.440
"I am Groot!"

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.800
"I am Steve Rogers."

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:42.150
If you really want to nitpick, Tony also never
met Howard the Duck, who shows up in the end

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:47.729
credits sequence of Guardians of the Galaxy,
but maybe that's for the best.

00:05:47.729 --> 00:05:52.819
We're pretty sure Tony's head would explode
coming up with a whole bunch of nicknames

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.690
for the talking duck.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:06:00.240
Even the most ambitious crossover event in
history couldn't get to everyone.

